# Review: CrxPlugin

The page-actions bridge is complete and well tested. `handleListEvent` and `handleInvokeEvent` implement every
ack code in the spec, including `disabled`, and `page-actions.test.ts` covers each failure path with a stub
invoker. The Composer e2e `crx.spec.ts` drives the real list and invoke events against a running app, using
plugin-github's action. The snapshot mappers match F-6 field by field and are unit-tested. The gaps are the
parts that touch the app shell: the success and error toasts, the auto-open after a clip, the settings form
and the three contributed picker actions have no test. QA-1 and QA-2 are not automated.

One prose divergence: the spec says the extension keeps a hand-validated mirror of the wire types at
`packages/apps/composer-crx/src/page-actions/types.ts`. That file no longer exists. Both sides import the
schemas from `@dxos/crx-protocol` (`PageAction.ts`), which plugin-crx re-exports from `src/types/PageAction.ts`.
The invoke handler also checks the `enabled` toggle before the version check, so a disabled bridge answers
`disabled` even to a version-2 request.

Of 51 items: 35 done, 8 untested, 5 partial, 0 diverged, 3 missing.

